                <pb facs="0465" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9596: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-23T13:00:00+08:00">August 23, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 23—8:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>538. My 530, August 21, 8 p.m.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d514-f1"/> Japanese military
                    at press conference this morning announced the arrival and landing “at several
                    places around Shanghai” during the night and early this morning of Japanese
                    troops. The above is confirmed by foreign military observers who believe that
                    Japanese troops are being landed at Woosung under cover of heavy naval barrage
                    and that landing has been made or is being attempted at Liuho approximately 15
                    miles up Yangtze River from Woosung. Exact number of troops not known but
                    estimates vary from 15 to 30,000.</p>
                <p>Military spokesman mentioned said that Japanese troops would immediately take the
                    offensive and attempt to cut off Chinese retreat. It is therefore probable that
                    large scale Japanese offensive operations will take place in and around Shanghai
                    within the next day or two unless the Chinese rapidly withdraw to prepared
                    positions said to be 25 or 30 miles west of Shanghai.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department, Nanking and Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
